/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pem
*.key
# Task 6 step 6 mints e2e/fixtures/signed/{public.pem,signing.pem} as CHECKED-IN
# test fixtures that Tasks 7, 13 and 14 read by path. Without this un-ignore,
# `git add -A` never stages them and a fresh CI checkout fails on a missing file.
!/e2e/fixtures/signed/*.pem
# Task 23: the org root's PUBLIC half, and only the public half. It is the
# bytes `third_party/org-root.fingerprint` is the SHA-256 of, so without this
# un-ignore the checked-in fingerprint would be 64 hex characters nobody could
# recompute. NO PRIVATE KEY IS EVER CHECKED IN HERE: the `*.key` line above
# stands, this un-ignore names exactly one public file, and the private half of
# that keypair was generated outside the tree and destroyed (docs/kubernetes.md
# §14).
!/third_party/org-root.pub.pem
/e2e/compose/.data
# The engine binary is extracted by scripts/extract-engine.sh, never committed;
# the vendored hedge is the tarball in third_party/ (Global Constraint 15).
/.engine/
# Generated by scripts/extract-engine.sh; must be regenerated, never checked in,
# so it cannot drift from third_party/kafka-backup-binary.digest.
/e2e/compose/.env
/third_party/*.tar.gz
!/third_party/.gitkeep
.env.local
.demo/
/upstream/
# Task 21c: the e2e suite's scratch directory — generated specs, approvals,
# per-run keys, the allowlist built from the LIVE cluster id, the scorecard the
# run wrote with --out, and the TMPDIR the engine container mounts. All of it is
# reproduced by running the suite; none of it is evidence.
/.e2e/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
